	(text "12 V OUTPUTS (decoder mode): ACC, illumination, reverse, spare"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6c7e5cab-e1ad-5d5a-be5f-90e43fa63519")
	)
	(text "After a processor reset the 100k resistor keeps the NPN transistor off: output off.\nThe 12 V Zener protects the P-MOSFET gate against surges. The switch works from about 5 V,\nso ACC holds during engine cranking (measured 7.16 V at cranking on the reference car).\nAlternatives: NPN any SOT-23 (BC817, BC847, MMBT3904, S8050 = marking J3Y); any 12 V 0.5 W Zener;\noutput diode SS14 / SS24 / 1N4148W; P-MOSFET SOT-23 min. 30 V with +/-20 V gate (AO3407, marking A7).\nZener: through-hole pads (two holes, 7.62 mm pitch), cathode to +12V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9b5df118-3bf2-5dae-ae38-1ea80ec4b9ad")
	)
